# PMRoo E2E testing (`y-tst-e2e-pmroo`)

Use this rule for **all** PMRoo (Property Manager) end-to-end manual test runs — especially **Context Capture**, **Action Request**, **mixed intent**, and **duplicate comment** bugs (e.g. [VAP-2752](https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-2752) under epic [VAP-3258](https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-3258)).

**Entry point:** When starting from **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e.mdc`**, answer Q0 with **PMRoo** first, then follow this rule. When PMRoo is already clear, invoke this rule **directly** (skip Q0).

Final report format: `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/insight/y-ins-e2e-report.mdc`.

Skill reference: [`.cursor/skills/roo-chat-testing/SKILL.md`](../../../.cursor/skills/roo-chat-testing/SKILL.md).

---

## Local-only default (current policy)

**Unless the user explicitly opts into remote MP Testing**, run PMRoo E2E entirely on localhost:

| Step | Command / target |
|------|------------------|
| Start mock stack | **`make mp-mock-e2e-up`** — starts `mp-mock`, recreates `roo` / `roo-worker` with `VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL=http://mp-mock:8099` ([`mp_mock/docker-compose.smoke.yml`](../../../mp_mock/docker-compose.smoke.yml)) |
| Chat API | **`http://localhost:8800/chat/api/chat`** (`docker-compose.dev.yml` maps `8800:8000`) |
| GenSearch DB | **`localhost:5432`** — `POSTGRES_DB_*` from repo **`.env`** |
| MP API (inside Roo) | **`http://mp-mock:8099`** (container) / **`http://localhost:8099`** (host sanity checks) |
| Tear down | **`make mp-mock-e2e-off`** — restores live `VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL` from **`.env`** for other work |

**Blocked by default during a local PMRoo run:**

- `api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai` chat API or Marketplace REST
- PM Web UI on testing MP
- n8n API / workflow triggers
- **Langfuse** — skip for local pass/fail; use chat JSON response + GenSearch SQL only
- Editing root **`.env`** or **`.env.e2e.local`** for mock mode

If a step would call testing MP, use mock seed data or stop and ask the user to opt into remote (Q1/Q2).

**Shared infra note:** `make mp-mock-e2e-up` is the same target ResiRoo uses — always run **`make mp-mock-e2e-off`** when finished so local `roo` is not left on mock for unrelated sessions.

